{"model":"gpt-6-luna","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are an orchestration agent.\nWhen repository inspection is needed and a suitable subagent exists, delegate the inspection.\nDo not use bash directly when `repo_inspector` can do the work.\nSummarize delegated findings clearly and briefly."},{"role":"user","content":"Inspect this repository by delegating the inspection to the `repo_inspector` subagent.\n\nRequirements for the delegated subagent work:\n- Use bash at least 3 separate times.\n- Do not combine commands with && or ;.\n- Run these as separate bash calls:\n  1. pwd\n  2. ls examples\/D05_AgentTroubleshooting\n  3. rg -n \"UseSubagents|SpawnSubagentTool|SubagentSpawning\" packages\/agents\/src\/Capability\/Subagent\/*.php packages\/agents\/src\/Events\/Subagent*.php\n\nThen answer in 3 short bullets:\n1. What kind of repository this is\n2. Where the agent telemetry examples live\n3. What the subagent telemetry path records"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_gL46FhHQ6RSYs0rf8GlKh6L2","type":"function","function":{"name":"spawn_subagent","arguments":"{\"subagent\":\"repo_inspector\",\"context\":\"fresh\",\"prompt\":\"Inspect the repository. You must use bash at least 3 separate times and do not combine commands with && or ;. Run each as a separate bash call, exactly: (1) pwd (2) ls examples\\\/D05_AgentTroubleshooting (3) rg -n \\\"UseSubagents|SpawnSubagentTool|SubagentSpawning\\\" packages\\\/agents\\\/src\\\/Capability\\\/Subagent\\\/*.php packages\\\/agents\\\/src\\\/Events\\\/Subagent*.php. Then investigate enough to answer: what kind of repository this is, where agent telemetry examples live, and what the subagent telemetry path records. Return concise evidence.\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_gL46FhHQ6RSYs0rf8GlKh6L2","content":"- **Repository:** A PHP project with an Agent SDK and first-party Laravel package; the README lists subagents and event observability among the SDK\u2019s features. (`README.md:9,13`)\n- **Examples:** Agent telemetry examples live in `examples\/D05_AgentTroubleshooting\/`: `TelemetryLangfuse`, `TelemetryLogfire`, `SubagentTelemetryLangfuse`, and `SubagentTelemetryLogfire`. (directory listing)\n- **Subagent telemetry:** `SpawnSubagentTool` emits spawn and completion events, and the examples bridge parent\/child events through `RuntimeEventBridge` and `AgentsTelemetryProjector`. The spawn event includes parent IDs, subagent name, prompt, and nesting depth; completion includes the subagent ID. (source and example matches)\n"}],"parallel_tool_calls":false,"max_completion_tokens":1024,"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command and return bounded stdout\/stderr. Use for shell operations, not file reading.\n\nExamples:\n- \"git status\" \u2192 check git state\n- \"composer install\" \u2192 install dependencies\n- \"php artisan migrate\" \u2192 run migrations\n- \"grep -r 'TODO' src\/\" \u2192 search file contents\n- \"npm run build\" \u2192 run build scripts\n\nPrefer dedicated file tools over cat, sed-based rewrites, and shell redirection.\nIf output is truncated, narrow the command or redirect it to a file and inspect it with the dedicated read tool.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"The bash command to execute"}},"required":["command"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"spawn_subagent","description":"Spawn a specialized subagent for a focused task. Returns only the final response.\n\nEach subagent has specific expertise, tools, and capabilities optimized for its domain.\nChoose the most appropriate subagent based on the task requirements.\n\nAvailable subagents:\n- repo_inspector: Inspects repository paths with bash and reports concise evidence (tools: bash)","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"subagent":{"type":"string","description":"Which subagent to spawn","enum":["repo_inspector"]},"prompt":{"type":"string","description":"The task or question for the subagent"},"context":{"type":"string","description":"fork reuses the captured parent context; fresh starts empty","enum":["fork","fresh"]}},"required":["subagent","prompt"],"additionalProperties":false}}}],"tool_choice":"auto","reasoning_effort":"none"}